# features/ — Feature Modules

## Overview

Each feature is a self-contained module following a consistent internal structure:

```
feature/
├── components/   → React components (pages, panels, UI)
├── context/      → React Context + useReducer state management
├── hooks/        → Custom hooks (persistence, navigation)
└── utils/        → Pure utility functions (projects only)
```

## Features

| Feature | Route | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| **auth** | N/A (modal) | User authentication (sign in, sign up, sign out) |
| **board** | `/` | Weekly task board with drag-and-drop columns |
| **documents** | `/documents` | Rich text document editor with tree navigation |
| **projects** | `/projects` | Project management with hierarchical tasks |

## Shared Patterns

- **Context + Reducer**: Each feature manages state via `useReducer` inside a Context provider.
- **Persistence hooks**: Each feature has a `usePersistence` hook that selects the right storage client (localStorage vs API) based on auth status.
- **Optimistic updates**: UI updates immediately; rolls back on API failure.
- **Toast notifications**: Errors surfaced via `react-hot-toast`.
- **Confirm dialogs**: Destructive actions require confirmation via `ConfirmDialog`.
